  "configuration_id": "config_040",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder (0.725 vs 0.52 for scgpt, 0.59 for pca_n2000), transformer aggregation (0.721 vs 0.715 for avgpool), and weighted fusion (0.725 vs 0.721 for concat). The current best (config_001, 0.725) uses imagenet_vit_l, but we have not yet tested resnet50 with this optimal combination of scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted in multiprofile. Config_040 directly tests whether the lighter ResNet50 image encoder can match or approach ViT-L performance under the best other settings. If it performs comparably, it offers a cheaper path to the same accuracy; if it underperforms, it confirms ViT-L is necessary. This is the highest-information experiment remaining: it resolves the last major unexplored axis (image encoder) for the proven-best configuration. Expected relative cost: ResNet50 is substantially smaller than ViT-L, so I estimate ~2.5–3.0 GPU hours, cheaper than config_001's 3.60 hours."
}

